  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 12, P = 23. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[9, 0, 18, 2, 22, 15, 11, 21, 15, 10, 17, 21], [13, 1, 10, 18, 6, 12, 9, 0, 21, 5, 4, 9], [5, 20, 11, 4, 5, 10, 21, 11, 15, 15, 9, 6]], sigma = [3, 10, 11, 0, 9, 7, 8, 5, 6, 4, 1, 2], B = [20, 13, 13, 20, 22, 16, 2, 16, 2, 22, 13, 13].",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2609.30069",
   "https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data"
  ],
  "date": "2026",
  "novelty": "known_parameters",
  "notes": "Literature baseline: a reproduction of a code published with arXiv:2609.30069, rebuilt from the authors' data repository (https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data/blob/306b31d/codes/reverse_fold/j3l12/specs/reverse_j3l12_p23_k71.json). Not a new construction. The authors report d = 6 as exact. Their lower-bound search output is not in the repository, so this entry carries an upper bound backed by their weight-6 Pauli logical, stored as the witness."
